"[2509.13311v1] Towards General Agentic Intelligence via Environment Scaling (https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.13311v1)\nciteturn3256view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.13311v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 160\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 16 Sep 2025]\nL9: # Title:Towards General Agentic Intelligence via Environment Scaling\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Runnan Fang , cite6†Shihao Cai , cite7†Baixuan Li , cite8†Jialong Wu , cite9†Guangyu Li , cite10†Wenbiao Yin , cite11†Xinyu Wang , cite11†Xiaobin Wang , cite12†Liangcai Su , cite13†Zhen Zhang , cite14†Shibin Wu , cite15†Zhengwei Tao , cite16†Yong Jiang , cite17†Pengjun Xie , cite18†Fei Huang , cite19†Jingren Zhou L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Towards General Agentic Intelligence via Environment Scaling, by Runnan Fang and 15 other authors\nL14: cite20†View PDF cite21†HTML (experimental) L15: > Abstract:Advanced agentic intelligence is a prerequisite for deploying Large Language Models in practical, real-world applications. Diverse real-world APIs demand precise, robust function-calling intelligence, which needs agents to develop these capabilities through interaction in varied environments. The breadth of function-calling competence is closely tied to the diversity of environments in which agents are trained.\nL16: In this work, we scale up environments as a step towards advancing general agentic intelligence. This gives rise to two central challenges: (i) how to scale environments in a principled manner, and (ii) how to effectively train agentic capabilities from experiences derived through interactions with these environments.\nL17: To address these, we design a scalable framework that automatically constructs heterogeneous environments that are fully simulated, systematically broadening the space of function-calling scenarios. We further adapt a two-phase agent fine-tuning strategy: first endowing agents with fundamental agentic capabilities, then specializing them for domain-specific contexts.\nL18: Extensive experiments on agentic benchmarks, tau-bench, tau2-Bench, and ACEBench, demonstrate that our trained model, AgentScaler, significantly enhances the function-calling capability of models.\nL19: Comments:  | cite22†this https URL†tongyi-agent.github.io L20: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite23†arXiv:2509.13311 [cs.CL]\nL22:    | (or cite24†arXiv:2509.13311v1 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL23:    | cite25†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2509.13311†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Jialong Wu [cite26†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Tue, 16 Sep 2025 17:57:20 UTC (1,024 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled Towards General Agentic Intelligence via Environment Scaling, by Runnan Fang and 15 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite20†View PDF L36:   * cite21†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite27†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite28†view license†creativecommons.org L40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.CL\nL43: \nL44: cite29†< prev |   cite30†next > L45: \nL46: cite31†new | cite32†recent | cite33†2025-09 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite34†cs L51: \nL52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * cite35†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L55:   * cite36†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L56:   * cite37†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L57: \nL58: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL59: \nL60: ## BibTeX formatted citatio